ach line IN file  \n            IF username AND password MATCH stored credentials  \n                RETURN True  \n        RETURN False  \n    END FUNCTION  \nEND CLASS  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask` (session management, request handling)  \n- `os` (file existence check)  \n\n---\n\n2. |Case|:navigate_to_registration  \nPseudocode:  \n```html\n<!-- login.html -->  \n<a href="{{ url_for(\'register\') }}">Register here</a>  \n\n<!-- register.html -->  \n<form method="POST">  \n    <input type="text" name="username" required>  \n    <input type="password" name="password" required>  \n    <input type="email" name="email" required>  \n    <button type="submit">Register</button>  \n</form>  \n```  \nKey Functionality:  \n- Simple HTML navigation via Flask routing (`url_for`).  \n\nPseudocode:  \n```\nROUTE /register  \n    RENDER register.html  \n\n<register.html>  \n    FORM action="/register" method="POST"  \n        INPUT username, password, email  \n        BUTTON submit  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask` (route handling, template rendering)  \n\nPseudocode:  \n```\n<a href="{{ url_for(\'register\') }}">Register here</a>  \n\nFUNCTION register()  \n    IF request.method == \'POST\'  \n        username = request.form[\'username\']  \n        password = request.form[\'password\']  \n        email = request.form[\'email\']  \n        IF UserManager.register_user(username, password, email)  \n            REDIRECT to login  \n        ELSE  \n            RENDER register.html WITH error="Registration failed"  \n    ELSE  \n        RENDER register.html  \nEND FUNCTION  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask` (routing, template rendering)  \n\n---\n\n3. ', '|Case|:user_registration  \nPseudocode:  \n```python\nFUNCTION register()  \n    IF request.method == \'POST\'  \n        username = request.form[\'username\']  \n        password = request.form[\'password\']  \n        email = request.form[\'email\']  \n        IF UserManager.register(username, password, email)  \n            REDIRECT to login()  \n        ELSE  \n            RENDER register.html WITH error="Username already exists"  \n        ENDIF  \n    ELSE  \n        RENDER register.html  \n    ENDIF  \nEND FUNCTION  \n\n# UserManager.register()  \nFUNCTION register(username, password, email)  \n    READ users.txt  \n    IF username EXISTS in file  \n        RETURN False  \n    APPEND new user (username|password|email) to users.txt  \n    RETURN True  \nEND FUNCTION  \n```  \nKey Functionality:  \n- Checks for duplicate usernames before registration.  \n- Stores credentials in plaintext (`users.txt`).  \n\nPseudocode:  \n```\nFUNCTION register_post()  \n    GET username, password, email FROM form  \n    CALL UserManager.register_user(username, password, email)  \n        IF any field EMPTY  \n            RETURN False  \n        APPEND username:password:email to users.txt  \n        RETURN True  \n    IF success  \n        REDIRECT to login  \n    ELSE  \n        REDIRECT to register  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `Flask` (form handling, file I/O)  \n\nPseudocode:  \n```\nCLASS UserManager  \n    FUNCTION register_user(username, password, email)  \n        IF username OR password OR email MISSING  \n            RETURN False  \n        APPEND new user to users.txt  \n        RETURN True  \n    END FUNCTION  \nEND CLASS  \n```\nKey Libraries:  \n- `os` (file handling)  \n\n---\n\n4. |Case|:view_current_tip  \nPseudocode:  \n```python\nFUNCTION main()  \n    IF \'username\' NOT IN session  \n        REDIRECT to login()  \n    current_tip = TipManager.get_current_tip()  \n    RENDER main.html WITH tip=current_tip  \nEND FUNCTION  \n\n# TipManager.get_current_tip()  \nFUNCTION get_current_tip()  \n    IF tips list NOT empty  \n        RETURN tips[current_index]  \n    RETURN None  \nEND FUNCTION  \n```  \nKey Functionality:  \n- Retrieves the first tip (`current_index = 0`) on initial load.  \n\nPseudocode:  \n```\nFUNCTION dashboard()  \n    CALL TipManager.get_current_tip()  \n      